{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-21-citation-lists/DESIGN.md | sed -n '154,280p'; nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-21-citation-lists/DESIGN.md | sed -n '19,41p;89,112p'\"","aggregated_output":"   154\t- D694: a new name for a request change.\n   155\t- D198: the closed set is what the request showed.\n   156\t- D358: the evidence-bloat halts, the same class.\n   157\t- D711: the census and the recommendation.\n   158\t- The pre-v74i extraction admission schema constrained `folds_into` to the shown ids. It was removed with the frozen prompt (commit\n   159\t  248ef1b4); no decision rejected it.\n   160\t\n   161\t## 5. The $0 test (registered before it runs)\n   162\t\n   163\t### T1: the product path\n   164\told-2 is replayed under poc-v121 through `replay.run`, serial path.\n   165\t- **The archive.** A scratch archive seeded with old-2's non-judge calls only, so every judge request misses it and reaches the\n   166\t  transport and the real validator.\n   167\t- **The transport.**\n   168\t  - It finds each judge request's stored old-2 call by its (system, user) bytes; the 1,620 pairs are unique (Codex r38).\n   169\t  - It asserts that the outgoing request equals the stored one in every key except the format.\n   170\t  - It asserts that the format has `strict: true` and the name `judgement`, and differs from v7's only in the four citation\n   171\t    constraints and the `$defs` they use.\n   172\t  - It asserts that each of the outgoing lists (evidence, dependencies, themes) equals the ids the request shows, read from its text\n   173\t    (evidence and theme entries; dependency entries).\n   174\t    - A mismatch is listed with its call and read by hand: a parser case is told from a builder bug before T1 can pass.\n   175\t    - An extra or missing id in any list fails T1. Codex r38c added an unlisted theme to 1,471 formats and every stored answer still\n   176\t      validated, so validation alone cannot catch it.\n   177\t  - It returns the stored answer, which goes through the real `model.call` and `model.check_schema`.\n   178\t  - Any other request (a non-judge miss, an unknown pair) stops the replay.\n   179\t- **The four refused first calls** (e88, e3955, e3998, theme ids). Each gets the saved accepted retry answer, labelled as a\n   180\t  substitution: under strict mode the provider could not have returned the refused one. All four retry answers fit their first\n   181\t  requests (Codex r38b). The four retry-note requests are not reached and are tested apart (T1b).\n   182\t- **Pass.**\n   183\t  - Exactly 1,616 judge responses through the transport, 4 of them labelled substitutions.\n   184\t  - The replay completes.\n   185\t  - The store equals old-2's on every table, listed explicitly from `sqlite_master`, with the expected differences named:\n   186\t    timestamps, archive call ids, request hashes, config checksum and version, and new empty tables.\n   187\t    - Judgements are compared on every substantive field: view, sequence, input, rung, reasons, reference, implied outcome, cites,\n   188\t      `cites_views`, pushes, theme pushes, changed, `why_changed`, publication day.\n   189\t    - Every other table is compared on all its columns but the named ones (handovers, match records, days completed and the rest).\n   190\t  - New request hashes and the config are checked apart.\n   191\t\n   192\tT1 does not touch provider acceptance (§6).\n   193\t\n   194\t### T1b: the four originals\n   195\tEach refused original goes through the real `model.call` under its v12 request and raises `SchemaError` on the id `check_answer`\n   196\trefused.\n   197\t\n   198\t### T1c: a real v12 retry\n   199\t- A store fixture with a theme in force; a fake provider answers the first v12 request with a duplicate theme push, which\n   200\t  `check_answer` refuses, then answers the retry correctly.\n   201\t- Assert that the retry request carries exactly the first request's format, citation lists included, and the retry note.\n   202\t- Mutant: the retry sent with the open v7 format must fail this test.\n   203\t\n   204\t### T5: preflight on a judge row without a saved format\n   205\tA refused judge row whose request has no `response_format` makes `scripts/preflight.py` exit non-zero, with the row named.\n   206\tToday `main` ignores part A's result, so it also needs a failing exit for this case. Extraction and matching rows keep their\n   207\tpaths.\n   208\t\n   209\t### T2: every stored shape, offline (evidence from archived text)\n   210\t- For every stored judge request of old-1, old-2, old-3, control-1 and linked-1, the lists are taken from the saved text. These are\n   211\t  archived calls whose store state is gone.\n   212\t- The parser can widen or narrow a list (the footnote case), so T2 is evidence from the archived text. T1 covers the built path.\n   213\t- Each answer is validated through the real `check_schema` with the v12 format.\n   214\t- Pass:\n   215\t  - all 5,389 committed answers and the 2 uncommitted valid ones validate;\n   216\t  - all 17 refused answers fail on their bad id;\n   217\t  - the population is printed as in §1.\n   218\t\n   219\t### T3: the real validator's controls\n   220\tFor all four fields, through `model.check_schema`:\n   221\t- an allowed id passes;\n   222\t- an unlisted id fails.\n   223\t\n   224\tAn empty list with `maxItems: 0` passes `[]`, and fails one otherwise valid item of the right type with an array-length error,\n   225\tnot a type error.\n   226\t\n   227\tT3 fails on today's validator, which ignores `maxItems`.\n   228\t\n   229\t### T3b: one owner of membership\n   230\t- A rendered request whose evidence quote holds a blank line followed by \"[1]\", with a real evidence entry after it. The v12 lists\n   231\t  include the later id, and `check_answer` under v12 accepts a citation of it.\n   232\t- The same answer under v7's text parser is refused. This control shows the parser case is real.\n   233\t\n   234\t### T4: sizes\n   235\tThe largest format over the five archives and over the sealed D358 archive is printed: evidence count, enum values with the\n   236\treference counted once and counted twice, and characters.\n   237\t\n   238\t### Mutants\n   239\tEach is caught by a test that passes on the unmutated code:\n   240\t- push ids left open;\n   241\t- lists parsed from the text instead of taken from the rows (the multiline-quote case);\n   242\t- `check_answer` under v12 reading the text instead of the lists (T3b);\n   243\t- `maxItems` dropped for an empty list;\n   244\t- `maxItems` removed from the validator;\n   245\t- `strict` dropped from the outgoing format (T1);\n   246\t- preflight reading the fixed schema for judge rows.\n   247\t\n   248\t### Also\n   249\t- Prompt size: the format's characters and tokens before and after, median and max.\n   250\t- The suite, the frozen tests and `docs/check.py`.\n   251\t\n   252\t## 6. What the $0 test cannot show\n   253\t\n   254\t- **Provider acceptance of the exact format:** the shared reference, `maxItems: 0`, and a largest request (D358 call 6918's size).\n   255\t- **Whether the judge picks the intended source when constrained:** e3111 could become e3110 or e3112.\n   256\t- **Whether the forecasts move.**\n   257\t\n   258\tA paid step, Alex's to open, settles these. It would first send the largest stored request and an empty-list request to check\n   259\tacceptance, then re-send the stored refused requests and a matched set of accepted ones, and read the cited sources beside the\n   260\tforecasts.\n    19\t\n    20\tv2 answers council round 38 (`codex-r38.md`): the format-error path, the batch and resume cells, duplicate theme pushes, preflight,\n    21\tthe D358 sizes, lists from the rendered rows, an unused version name, and the T1 proof.\n    22\t\n    23\tv3 answers round 38b (`codex-r38b.md`):\n    24\t- one owner of membership: under v12, `check_answer` uses the same row-built lists;\n    25\t- preflight reads the saved format of judge rows only;\n    26\t- the v7/v8 path keeps calling `build_prompt`;\n    27\t- a format error on the retry;\n    28\t- `maxItems: 0` keeps the item types;\n    29\t- T1's exact assertions;\n    30\t- T2 described as evidence from archived text, with a footnote control.\n    31\t\n    32\t## 1. Census (stored data, $0)\n    33\t\n    34\t- **Refusals.** Every refused judge answer on the stored runs is an id-membership error: an id outside the list its field allows.\n    35\t  - Population (Codex r37b and r38, reproduced by Claude's `id_typo_census.py`): 5,415 archive rows, 5,408 distinct request-answer\n    36\t    pairs, 5,389 committed, 17 refused, 2 valid answers of the stopped control batch never committed. Sources: old-1, old-2, old-3,\n    37\t    and the pilots' fresh rows.\n    38\t  - The classes:\n    39\t    - a one-character copy of a listed evidence id (e3620 → e362);\n    40\t    - a garbled evidence id (`e393`);\n    41\t    - a theme id in `cites_views` or in an evidence field;\n    89\t- **The format.**\n    90\t  - One `$defs` string enum of the evidence ids, sorted, referenced by `cites.items` and `pushes.items.evidence_id`.\n    91\t  - A plain enum of the dependency ids for `cites_views.items`.\n    92\t  - A plain enum of the theme ids for `theme_pushes.items.view_id`.\n    93\t  - An empty list gives its array `maxItems: 0` and keeps its item type: a string for `cites` and `cites_views`; the full object for\n    94\t    `pushes` and `theme_pushes`, with its id field an open string. No empty enum is written.\n    95\t  - The schema name stays `judgement`.\n    96\t- **The local validator** (`model.check_schema`) gains `maxItems`, the mirror of `minItems`. No existing schema uses it (grep), so\n    97\t  no current answer changes status.\n    98\t- **Preflight part A**, judge rows only, checks each stored refused row against the format saved in that row's request\n    99\t  (`request_json.response_format.json_schema.schema`).\n   100\t  - A judge row without a saved format is reported as such, not skipped.\n   101\t  - Extraction and matching rows keep their current paths. A Jev row's request has no `response_format` (Codex r38b).\n   102\t- **Size.**\n   103\t  - No pre-send counting rule: the provider's counting of a referenced enum is unverified, and a guessed rule could refuse a\n   104\t    request the provider accepts.\n   105\t  - A request the provider refuses comes back as HTTP 400, which the transport raises at once without retrying (`openai_transport`).\n   106\t    It goes through `judge_day`'s generic path to `judging_failed`, and the day is resumable. A resume sends the same oversized\n   107\t    request and hits the same limit; that visible stop is the behaviour until a design change.\n   108\t  - No rule drops evidence to fit.\n   109\t\n   110\t## 4. Tables\n   111\t\n   112\t### 4.1 State × event\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba src/hivemind/views/judging.py | sed -n '199,246p;329,352p'; nl -ba scripts/preflight.py | sed -n '59,73p;326,348p'; nl -ba src/hivemind/model.py | sed -n '245,286p'\"","aggregated_output":"   199\tdef retry_note(errors):\n   200\t    return '\\n\\nThe code returned the previous answer because: ' + '; '.join(errors) + '\\nCorrect it and answer again, citing only the listed ids.'\n   201\t\n   202\t\n   203\tdef themes_shown_in(request_text):\n   204\t    \"\"\"The theme ids of the block a request carried: the ids the answer may name, whatever the ledger says now.\"\"\"\n   205\t    block = request_text.split('\\n[Themes in force, ', 1)\n   206\t    return set(re.findall(r'^- (v\\d+) \\(', block[1].split('\\n\\n[', 1)[0], re.M)) if len(block) == 2 else set()\n   207\t\n   208\t\n   209\tdef evidence_shown_in(request_text):\n   210\t    \"\"\"The evidence ids the request listed: the ids the answer may cite and push.\"\"\"\n   211\t    block = request_text.split('\\n[Evidence in ', 1)\n   212\t    return set(re.findall(r'^- (e\\d+) \\[', block[1].split('\\n\\n[', 1)[0], re.M)) if len(block) == 2 else set()\n   213\t\n   214\t\n   215\tdef check_answer(conn, view_id, data, request_text=None):\n   216\t    \"\"\"request_text: the user message that was sent, so theme and evidence ids are checked against what it carried (a theme may have\n   217\t    closed or opened since); without it, against what the ledger would show now.\"\"\"\n   218\t    errors = []\n   219\t    shown = themes_shown_in(request_text) if request_text is not None else {theme['view_id'] for theme in themes_in_force(conn, view_id)}\n   220\t    named = []\n   221\t    for entry in data.get('theme_pushes', []):\n   222\t        if entry['view_id'] in named:\n   223\t            errors.append(f'{entry[\"view_id\"]} is named twice in theme_pushes')\n   224\t        elif entry['view_id'] not in shown:\n   225\t            errors.append(f'{entry[\"view_id\"]} is not a theme in force shown to {view_id}')\n   226\t        named.append(entry['view_id'])\n   227\t    # the closed set is what the request showed (D198), read from the text that was sent, else computed from the ledger\n   228\t    allowed = evidence_shown_in(request_text) if request_text is not None else {p['evidence_id'] for p in evidence_in_view(conn, view_id)[0]}\n   229\t    not_allowed = lambda e: f'{e} is not among the evidence shown to {view_id}'\n   230\t    bad_push = lambda e: f'push on {e} which was not shown to {view_id}'\n   231\t    deps = {d['resolved_to'] for d in store.dependencies_of(conn, view_id) if d['resolved_to']}\n   232\t    rungs = store.rungs_of(conn, view_id)\n   233\t    if not 1 <= data['rung'] <= len(rungs):\n   234\t        errors.append(f'rung {data[\"rung\"]} outside 1..{len(rungs)}')\n   235\t    for cited in data['cites']:\n   236\t        if cited not in allowed:\n   237\t            errors.append(not_allowed(cited))\n   238\t    for cited in data['cites_views']:\n   239\t        if cited not in deps:\n   240\t            errors.append(f'{cited} is not a dependency of {view_id}')\n   241\t    for push in data['pushes']:\n   242\t        if push['evidence_id'] not in allowed:\n   243\t            errors.append(bad_push(push['evidence_id']))\n   244\t    for field in STANCE_FIELDS:\n   245\t        if not str(data.get(field) or '').strip():\n   246\t            errors.append(f'{field} is empty: state what the market expects and the figure or date the evidence implies')\n   329\t    while pending:\n   330\t        ready = [v for v in pending if upstream(conn, v).isdisjoint(set(pending) - {v})] or pending[:1]\n   331\t        level = [v for v in ready if is_theme(v)] or ready\n   332\t        prompts = {v: build_prompt(conn, v, version) for v in level}\n   333\t\n   334\t        def ask(view_id, note=''):\n   335\t            system, user = prompts[view_id]\n   336\t            return model.call(archive, cfg, cfg.rejudging, system, user + note, schema, 'judgement', 'judge', transport=transport)\n   337\t\n   338\t        with concurrent.futures.ThreadPoolExecutor(max_workers=JUDGE_WORKERS) as pool_:\n   339\t            answers = dict(zip(level, pool_.map(ask, level)))\n   340\t        for view_id in level:\n   341\t            answer = answers[view_id]\n   342\t            errors = check_answer(conn, view_id, answer.data, prompts[view_id][1])\n   343\t            if errors:\n   344\t                archive.retire(answer.call_id)                 # a refused answer never answers the same request again (a resume re-samples)\n   345\t                answer = ask(view_id, retry_note(errors))\n   346\t                errors = check_answer(conn, view_id, answer.data, prompts[view_id][1])\n   347\t                if errors:\n   348\t                    archive.retire(answer.call_id)\n   349\t                    raise JudgementRefused(f'{view_id}: ' + '; '.join(errors))\n   350\t            result = _record(conn, cfg, view_id, seq, item, answer)\n   351\t            done.add(view_id)\n   352\t            results.append(result)\n    59\tdef part_a(archive_conn):\n    60\t    reasons, examples, judged = collections.Counter(), collections.defaultdict(list), 0\n    61\t    rows = archive_conn.execute(\"select purpose, request_sha256, answer_json from model_calls where request_sha256 like '%:schema:%' or request_sha256 like '%:malformed:%' or request_sha256 like '%:refused:%'\")\n    62\t    for purpose, sha, answer_json in (tuple(r) for r in rows):\n    63\t        judged += 1\n    64\t        if ':malformed:' in sha or not answer_json:\n    65\t            reasons[f'{purpose}: not JSON'] += 1\n    66\t            continue\n    67\t        for error in model.check_schema(json.loads(answer_json), SCHEMAS.get(purpose, {})):\n    68\t            key = f'{purpose}: {normalise_reason(error)}'\n    69\t            reasons[key] += 1\n    70\t            examples[key].append(error[:140])\n    71\t    tally('A. answers the schema refused (prompt/schema disagreements; empty when the provider enforces the schema server-side)', judged, judged, reasons, examples)\n    72\t    return judged\n    73\t\n   326\tdef main():\n   327\t    parser = argparse.ArgumentParser()\n   328\t    frozen_draw = os.path.join(ROOT, 'poc', 'data', 'e2e-r9-frozen-v108-2026-11-03', 'd1')\n   329\t    parser.add_argument('--archive', default=os.path.join(frozen_draw, 'archive.sqlite'))\n   330\t    parser.add_argument('--items', default=os.path.join(ROOT, 'poc', 'data', 'items-nvda-2026-07-01-10-27.sqlite'))\n   331\t    parser.add_argument('--views', nargs='*', default=None)\n   332\t    parser.add_argument('--universe', default=os.path.join(ROOT, 'poc', 'universe.json'))\n   333\t    args = parser.parse_args()\n   334\t    views_paths = args.views or [os.path.join(frozen_draw, 'views.sqlite')]\n   335\t    archive_conn = sqlite3.connect(f'file:{args.archive}?mode=ro', uri=True)\n   336\t    archive_conn.row_factory = sqlite3.Row\n   337\t    items_conn = testdb.open_db(args.items)\n   338\t    uni = universe.load(args.universe)\n   339\t    print('preflight over', args.archive, 'and', len(views_paths), 'views databases:', ', '.join(os.path.basename(os.path.dirname(p)) for p in views_paths))\n   340\t    part_a(archive_conn)\n   341\t    copies = store_copies(views_paths)\n   342\t    counts = [part_b(archive_conn, items_conn, uni), part_c(archive_conn, copies, uni), part_d()]\n   343\t    part_e(copies)          # informational for unkeyed ledgers; judged counts are reported per ledger\n   344\t    if min(counts) == 0:\n   345\t        print('\\nUNEXERCISED: a check judged no case')\n   346\t        sys.exit(1)\n   347\t    print('\\npreflight done')\n   348\t\n   245\tdef request_identity(request):\n   246\t    \"\"\"The exact serialized request and its archive key, shared by callers and validation.\"\"\"\n   247\t    encoded = json.dumps(request, sort_keys=True, ensure_ascii=False)\n   248\t    return encoded, hashlib.sha256(encoded.encode('utf-8')).hexdigest()\n   249\t\n   250\t\n   251\tdef call(archive, cfg, setting, system, user, schema, schema_name, purpose, *, transport=None):\n   252\t    provider = cfg.provider\n   253\t    request = build_request(setting, system, user, schema, schema_name, provider)\n   254\t    request_json, sha = request_identity(request)\n   255\t    hit = archive.lookup(sha)\n   256\t    prompt_chars = len(system) + len(user)\n   257\t    if hit:\n   258\t        call_id, answer_json, _, input_tokens, output_tokens = hit\n   259\t        return Answer(json.loads(answer_json), call_id, sha, True, prompt_chars, input_tokens or 0, output_tokens or 0, 0.0)\n   260\t    started = time.time()\n   261\t    response = (transport or openai_transport)(provider, request)\n   262\t    seconds = round(time.time() - started, 1)\n   263\t    try:\n   264\t        content = response['choices'][0]['message']['content']\n   265\t        data = json.loads(content)\n   266\t    except (KeyError, IndexError, TypeError, json.JSONDecodeError) as error:\n   267\t        archive.record(purpose=purpose, config_version=cfg.version, config_checksum=cfg.checksum, model=setting.model,\n   268\t                       request_sha256=sha + ':malformed:' + uuid.uuid4().hex[:8], request_json=request_json,\n   269\t                       response_json=json.dumps(response)[:200000], answer_json=None, prompt_chars=prompt_chars,\n   270\t                       input_tokens=0, output_tokens=0, cost_usd=0.0, seconds=seconds, created_at=time.strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%S'))\n   271\t        raise SchemaError(f'malformed answer: {error}')\n   272\t    errors = check_schema(data, schema)\n   273\t    usage = response.get('usage') or {}\n   274\t    input_tokens = int(usage.get('prompt_tokens') or 0)\n   275\t    output_tokens = int(usage.get('completion_tokens') or 0)\n   276\t    cached_tokens = min(input_tokens, int((usage.get('prompt_tokens_details') or {}).get('cached_tokens') or 0))\n   277\t    price_in, price_out = PRICES.get(setting.model, (0.0, 0.0))\n   278\t    cost = round((input_tokens - cached_tokens) / 1e6 * price_in + cached_tokens / 1e6 * price_in * CACHED_INPUT_SHARE + output_tokens / 1e6 * price_out, 6)\n   279\t    call_id = archive.record(purpose=purpose, config_version=cfg.version, config_checksum=cfg.checksum, model=setting.model,\n   280\t                             request_sha256=sha if not errors else sha + ':schema:' + uuid.uuid4().hex[:8], request_json=request_json,\n   281\t                             response_json=json.dumps(response)[:200000], answer_json=json.dumps(data, ensure_ascii=False),\n   282\t                             prompt_chars=prompt_chars, input_tokens=input_tokens, output_tokens=output_tokens, cost_usd=cost,\n   283\t                             seconds=seconds, created_at=time.strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%S'))\n   284\t    if errors:\n   285\t        raise SchemaError('; '.join(errors[:5]))\n   286\t    return Answer(data, call_id, sha, False, prompt_chars, input_tokens, output_tokens, cost)\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
